.TH FSTRACE-DAEMON 1 "2026-07-06" "fstrace 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fstrace-daemon \- privileged eBPF daemon for fstrace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fstrace-daemon
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B fstrace-daemon
.RB [ -h | --help ]
.RB [ -V | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fstrace-daemon
is the privileged half of
.BR fstrace (1).
It loads and attaches the eBPF programs once, owns the kernel ring buffer and
the traced\-pid map, and serves multiple unprivileged
.BR fstrace (1)
clients over a Unix socket.
.PP
Each client registers the pid of its stopped child; the daemon starts tracing
that pid and streams the resulting kernel events \(em and those of the child's
descendants \(em back to the owning client. It routes events by their
root\-namespace pid and never inspects
.IR /proc ,
so it remains correct even when run in a different pid and mount namespace than
its clients (for example, containerized with the socket bind\-mounted to the
host).
.PP
This is the only component that requires elevated privileges
.RB ( CAP_BPF
and
.BR CAP_PERFMON ,
or
.BR CAP_SYS_ADMIN );
the
.BR fstrace (1)
client runs as an ordinary user. The daemon runs in the foreground until
killed; use a service manager, or background it, to keep it running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Listen on the Unix socket
.IR PATH .
Overrides
.BR FSTRACE_SOCKET .
Defaults to
.BR /run/fstrace/fstrace.sock .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH SOCKET ACTIVATION
The daemon implements the systemd
.BR sd_listen_fds (3)
protocol. If launched via socket activation \(em with
.B LISTEN_FDS
and
.B LISTEN_PID
set \(em it adopts the listening socket systemd already bound and passed to it;
otherwise it binds the socket itself. Ready\-to\-use
.B fstrace.socket
and
.B fstrace.service
units, an init script, and a container image ship under
.IR packaging/ .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FSTRACE_SOCKET
Socket path to bind (default
.BR /run/fstrace/fstrace.sock ).
The
.B \-\-socket
option takes precedence. Must match the clients.
.TP
.B FSTRACE_PROFILE
Set to
.B 1
in both the daemon and client environments to emit aggregate daemon, client,
and eBPF performance summaries through the logging destination.
.TP
.BR FSTRACE_LOG_FILE ", " FSTRACE_LOG_DIR
Write log output to an explicit file, or to a per\-process file
.RI ( fstrace-daemon.log )
under a directory, respectively.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log verbosity using
.BR tracing / env\-filter
syntax, e.g.
.BR fstrace=trace .
.B FSTRACE_DEBUG=1
is shorthand for
.BR fstrace=debug .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Runs until killed. Exits
.B 0
on a clean shutdown and
.B 1
on a fatal startup error (for example, if the eBPF programs cannot be loaded),
printing a diagnostic to standard error. Exits
.B 2
on an invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the daemon (backgrounded) and then trace without
.BR sudo :
.PP
.RS
.B sudo fstrace-daemon &
.br
.B fstrace ls 3>&1
.RE
.PP
Run a private daemon on a custom socket:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo fstrace-daemon --socket /tmp/fst.sock &
.br
.B FSTRACE_SOCKET=/tmp/fst.sock fstrace ls 3>&1
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fstrace (1),
.BR sd_listen_fds (3)
.PP
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/bmiddha/fstrace
.UE
.SH AUTHOR
Bharat Middha and contributors.
